      "script": "<p>So that is the whole workbook. Three sheets, and the same rhythm every time: information, lookups, lab reference, and then the orange columns that belong to you.</p> <p>Three things to take away. <b>First</b>, by the twenty-fourth of April: check your region, surveyor and survey window on the site sheet, and confirm the uploader on the uploads sheet.</p> <p><b>Second</b>, before you set off for any site, filter on Ready to Visit. If it is not marked Yes, access is not through yet, and you would be making that trip twice.</p> <p><b>Third</b>, every site needs a clear Pass or Fail in the final result column, within your survey window.</p> <p>And if you get stuck on a specific site, the coordinator's name is right there on the row — please go to them directly. That is everything from me. Any questions on the workbook before we move on?</p>",
